DESCRIPTION:<b>REGISTRATION</b>: <a href="https://forms.cloud.microsoft/Pa
 ges/ResponsePage.aspx?id=TsVyyzFKnk2xSh6jbfrJTI9QJhcY12JAolV5CeByrWpUQlJM
 NUk5RDNVNFhHMDBPTTNRNkxXVTNHWS4u" target="_blank">Click Here</a>\n\n<i>NO
 TE: Registration closes 24 hours before event start. Please register ahea
 d of the event. Registrants will receive Zoom information and related mat
 erials by email one week and within 24 hours before the event.</i>\n\nRes
 erve your seat in the virtual Research Integrity Roundtable <i>Much Ado A
 bout Peer Review</i> on April 20th from 2:30-4:00 pm. Participants will l
 earn about the strengths and shortcomings of the peer review process\, po
 tential alternative processes for maintaining high-quality published rese
 arch\, and what kind of role AI should or should not have in the peer rev
 iew process. A case study will be discussed in breakout rooms.\n\nThis ev
 ent is only open to current Duke faculty\, staff\, and students. Particip
 ation in this event fulfills the <b>RCR-200</b> requirement for Faculty a
 nd Staff and the <b>714 RCR credit</b> for graduate students\, but partic
 ipants must attend for 60 minutes and participate in breakout room discus
 sion to receive credit.
DURATION:PT1H30M
DTSTAMP:20260127T190332Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260420T143000
LAST-MODIFIED:20260127T190332Z
