CREATED:20260324T194624Z
DESCRIPTION:The First-Year Experience extends beyond individual courses to
  foster community\, belonging\, and applied learning. David Schanzer (Pub
 lic Policy)\, Eileen Chow (Asian and Middle Eastern Studies)\, Dan Scolni
 c (Physics)\, and Nicole Schramm-Sapyta (Duke Institute for Brain Science
 s) will discuss how they design experiential components that deepen acade
 mic inquiry and build lasting connections.\n\nPanelists will reflect on:\
 n\n- Connecting experiential activities directly to course themes and int
 ellectual goals\n- Designing high-impact engagements that complement (rat
 her than compete with) coursework\n- Creating opportunities for sustained
  interaction across the first year and beyond\n- Partnering with Duke uni
 ts\, centers\, and community resources to enrich student learning
DURATION:PT1H
DTSTAMP:20260324T194624Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260420T150000
LAST-MODIFIED:20260324T194624Z
